# Data table

Sort, filter (by department) and paginate a table of employees, with
`keyed by` so a row's identity survives being reordered.

## Note

The rows on screen are one derived field, `visibleRows`: the employees filtered by department,
sorted by the chosen column and sliced to the current page. Every action changes only the field it
owns — `dept`, `sortKey`, `ascending` or `page` — and the table follows.

## An Employee has:
    an id, which is Int.
    a name, which is Text.
    a department, which is Text.
    a salaryCents, which is Int.

## To seedEmployees () -> Seq of Employee:
    Let mutable out be a new Seq of Employee.
    Push (a new Employee with id 1 and name "Grace" and department "Engineering" and salaryCents 950000) to out.
    Push (a new Employee with id 2 and name "Ada" and department "Engineering" and salaryCents 990000) to out.
    Push (a new Employee with id 3 and name "Barbara" and department "Sales" and salaryCents 780000) to out.
    Push (a new Employee with id 4 and name "Katherine" and department "Research" and salaryCents 860000) to out.
    Push (a new Employee with id 5 and name "Hedy" and department "Research" and salaryCents 910000) to out.
    Push (a new Employee with id 6 and name "Margaret" and department "Sales" and salaryCents 820000) to out.
    Push (a new Employee with id 7 and name "Radia" and department "Engineering" and salaryCents 875000) to out.
    Return out.

## To matchesDept (e: Employee) and (dept: Text) -> Bool:
    If dept is equal to "all":
        Return true.
    Return e's department is equal to dept.

## To filterByDept (rows: Seq of Employee) and (dept: Text) -> Seq of Employee:
    Let mutable out be a new Seq of Employee.
    Repeat for e in rows:
        If matchesDept(e, dept):
            Push e to out.
    Return out.

## To isBefore (a: Employee) and (b: Employee) and (sortKey: Text) and (ascending: Bool) -> Bool:
    Let mutable before be false.
    If sortKey is equal to "id":
        Set before to a's id is less than b's id.
    Otherwise:
        Set before to a's salaryCents is less than b's salaryCents.
    If ascending:
        Return before.
    Return not before.

## To sortRows (rows: Seq of Employee) and (sortKey: Text) and (ascending: Bool) -> Seq of Employee:
    Let mutable out be a new Seq of Employee.
    Repeat for e in rows:
        Let mutable insertAt be length of out.
        Let mutable i be 0.
        While i is less than length of out:
            If isBefore(e, item (i + 1) of out, sortKey, ascending):
                Set insertAt to i.
                Break.
            Set i to i + 1.
        Push e to out.
        Let mutable j be length of out.
        While j is greater than insertAt + 1:
            Let tmp be item (j - 1) of out.
            Set item (j - 1) of out to item j of out.
            Set item j of out to tmp.
            Set j to j - 1.
    Return out.

## To pageSlice (rows: Seq of Employee) and (pageNum: Int) and (perPage: Int) -> Seq of Employee:
    Let total be length of rows.
    Let clamped be clampPage(pageNum, total, perPage).
    Let mutable out be a new Seq of Employee.
    Let start be pageStart(clamped, perPage).
    Let stop be pageEnd(clamped, perPage, total).
    Let mutable i be start.
    While i is at most stop:
        Push item i of rows to out.
        Set i to i + 1.
    Return out.

## To dollars (cents: Int) -> Text:
    Return "${cents / 100}".

## Page /

State:
    Let rows be a new Seq of Employee.
    Let dept be "all".
    Let sortKey be "id".
    Let ascending be true.
    Let page be 1.
    Let perPage be 2.
    Let visibleRows always be pageSlice(sortRows(filterByDept(rows, dept), sortKey, ascending), page, perPage).

Actions:
    When the page loads:
        Set rows to seedEmployees().

    To setDept (d: Text):
        Set dept to d.
        Set page to 1.

    To sortById:
        If sortKey is equal to "id":
            Set ascending to not ascending.
        Otherwise:
            Set sortKey to "id".
            Set ascending to true.

    To sortBySalary:
        If sortKey is equal to "salary":
            Set ascending to not ascending.
        Otherwise:
            Set sortKey to "salary".
            Set ascending to true.

    To nextPage:
        Set page to page + 1.

    To prevPage:
        Set page to page - 1.

View:
    <nav class="filters">
        <button id="dept-all" class:active={dept is equal to "all"} on-click={setDept("all")}>All</button>
        <button id="dept-eng" class:active={dept is equal to "Engineering"} on-click={setDept("Engineering")}>Engineering</button>
        <button id="dept-sales" class:active={dept is equal to "Sales"} on-click={setDept("Sales")}>Sales</button>
        <button id="dept-research" class:active={dept is equal to "Research"} on-click={setDept("Research")}>Research</button>
    </nav>
    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th><button id="sort-id" on-click={sortById}>#</button></th>
                <th>Name</th>
                <th>Department</th>
                <th><button id="sort-salary" on-click={sortBySalary}>Salary</button></th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            {for each e in visibleRows, keyed by e's id:}
                <tr id="row-{e's id}">
                    <td class="name">{e's name}</td>
                    <td class="dept">{e's department}</td>
                    <td class="salary">{dollars(e's salaryCents)}</td>
                </tr>
            {else:}
                <tr class="empty"><td colspan="3">No employees match.</td></tr>
            {end}
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <nav class="pager">
        <button id="prev" on-click={prevPage}>Prev</button>
        <span id="page-num">Page {page}</span>
        <button id="next" on-click={nextPage}>Next</button>
    </nav>

Style:
    .filters button.active, .pager button.active { font-weight: 700; }
    table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }
    th, td { text-align: left; padding: .3rem .6rem; }

## Test: the table shows the first page sorted by id

Expect that the count of "tbody tr" is equal to 2.
Expect that the text of "#row-1 .name" is equal to "Grace".
Expect that the text of "#row-2 .name" is equal to "Ada".
Expect that the text of "#page-num" is equal to "Page 1".

## Test: paging moves to the next set of rows, keyed rows keep their identity

Click "#next".
Expect that the text of "#page-num" is equal to "Page 2".
Expect that the count of "tbody tr" is equal to 2.
Expect that the text of "#row-3 .name" is equal to "Barbara".
Expect that the text of "#row-4 .name" is equal to "Katherine".
Click "#next".
Expect that the text of "#page-num" is equal to "Page 3".
Expect that the count of "tbody tr" is equal to 2.
Expect that the text of "#row-5 .name" is equal to "Hedy".
Expect that the text of "#row-6 .name" is equal to "Margaret".
Click "#prev".
Expect that the text of "#page-num" is equal to "Page 2".
Expect that the text of "#row-3 .name" is equal to "Barbara".

## Test: sorting by salary, descending on a second click

Click "#sort-salary".
Expect that the count of "tbody tr" is equal to 2.
Expect that the text of "#row-3 .name" is equal to "Barbara".
Expect that the text of "#row-6 .name" is equal to "Margaret".
Click "#sort-salary".
Expect that the text of "#row-2 .name" is equal to "Ada".
Expect that the text of "#row-1 .name" is equal to "Grace".

## Test: filtering by department narrows the rows and resets to page one

Click "#dept-sales".
Expect that the count of "tbody tr" is equal to 2.
Expect that the text of "#row-3 .name" is equal to "Barbara".
Expect that the text of "#row-6 .name" is equal to "Margaret".
Expect that the text of "#page-num" is equal to "Page 1".

## Test: sorting by id toggles direction, and filtering to Research then back to all

Click "#sort-id".
Expect that the text of "#row-7 .name" is equal to "Radia".
Expect that the text of "#row-6 .name" is equal to "Margaret".
Click "#sort-id".
Expect that the text of "#row-1 .name" is equal to "Grace".
Expect that the text of "#row-2 .name" is equal to "Ada".
Click "#dept-research".
Expect that the count of "tbody tr" is equal to 2.
Expect that the text of "#row-4 .name" is equal to "Katherine".
Expect that the text of "#row-5 .name" is equal to "Hedy".
Click "#dept-all".
Expect that the count of "tbody tr" is equal to 2.
Expect that the text of "#row-1 .name" is equal to "Grace".

## Test: a department with more rows than fit still paginates

Click "#dept-eng".
Expect that the count of "tbody tr" is equal to 2.
Expect that the text of "#row-1 .name" is equal to "Grace".
Expect that the text of "#row-2 .name" is equal to "Ada".
Click "#next".
Expect that the count of "tbody tr" is equal to 1.
Expect that the text of "#row-7 .name" is equal to "Radia".
